Reason: design review 2026-11-09 A4 item 4 (roadmap P2-6). Mandatory rule 1 of CLAUDE.md states the spike-era write rule (localhost, config.json, scripts/common.py) as the general rule, next to the pls rule. This patch keeps the headline and every restriction: the spike wording is scoped to spike/round-trip/, and a new line keeps "role dev + operator opt-in" for every other write path (browser runner, ad-hoc scripts); the stg allowance stays only in the existing pls bullet. CLAUDE.md Mandatory is a protected path: Nam applies and commits it, or rejects it.

